Local-only: drop nixVulkanIntel's false LD_LIBRARY_PATH warning.

The script does not overwrite LD_LIBRARY_PATH — it prepends its own library
paths and preserves the inherited value:

    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<nix libs>"${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"

The warning dates from a version that did overwrite. It is printed on every
invocation, so it heads every e2e log, and it has already caused one wrong
diagnosis (a Vulkan loader problem attributed to a clobbered library path).

Applies to the mesa/Intel wrapper only; the NVIDIA wrapper has no such warning.
Independent of nixgl-nvidia-595.patch — no shared hunks, order does not matter.

--- a/nixGL.nix
+++ b/nixGL.nix
@@ -179,9 +179,6 @@
           + ''cat f | xargs | sed "s/ /:/g" > $out'');
       in ''
         #!${runtimeShell}
-        if [ -n "$LD_LIBRARY_PATH" ]; then
-          echo "Warning, nixVulkanIntel overwriting existing LD_LIBRARY_PATH" 1>&2
-        fi
         export VK_LAYER_PATH=${vulkan-validation-layers}/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d
         ICDS=$(cat ${icd})
         export VK_ICD_FILENAMES=$ICDS"''${VK_ICD_FILENAMES:+:$VK_ICD_FILENAMES}"
